# the app instance folder of the demonstration doc page
# (doc_page_impl_service.md). trying the Services tab creates app
# instances here: each one a copy of its template with its own service.yaml,
# and with its data (notes.sqlite) once it ran, when it keeps any of its own
# (an app service keeps it in an infra service instead). everything new is
# ignored; only the files of the instances listed below are part of the
# example.
# their data, their dashboard builds, installed dependencies and the record
# the kernel keeps of them (service-record.yaml) stay ignored.
# to add an instance to the example on purpose, list its folder here.

*
!*/
!/.gitignore

!/note-db-inst-w4veemd7i36/**
!/note-db-inst-w4veemdrx8y/**
# the todo-list instance of service-kernel.md: an app service whose data is
# a database of the sqlite infra instance (example_doc/service-infra/, ignored)
!/todo-list-inst-w55j3ztn3rq/**
/*/*.sqlite
/*/*.sqlite-journal
/*/service-record.yaml
/*/dashboard/dist/
/*/dashboard/node_modules/
/*/dashboard/package-lock.json
/*/__pycache__/
